## Attack 3 — is TestDashboardAndMCPProjectionAgree genuinely cross-path?
Yes. Traced the helpers: the MCP side calls cs.CallTool over a real
mcp.NewInMemoryTransports() client/server pair (register_test.go:62-81,
Register(srv, deps) is the production registration function) -- a real
protocol round-trip, not a direct function call. The dashboard side calls
dashboard.RegisterRoutes + chi router + httptest, i.e. the real HTTP handler
and template renderer. Both consume the SAME underlying *dataloader.DataLoader
and *storage.Storage (same tmp dir), which is the point -- they must
independently agree on the same data through two structurally different
entry points. Not a case of two thin wrappers around one call.

